  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the net estate exceeding Five million pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The net estate is determined by deducting allowable deductions from the gross estate. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the net estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis means that estates valued at ₱5,000,000 or less are exempt from estate tax, while estates valued above this threshold will incur a tax liability calculated at 6% of the amount exceeding ₱5,000,000. This change simplifies the estate tax structure and provides a clearer threshold for tax liability.",
